    "id": "task1",
    "chapterId": "ch_7",
    "title": "Create an Accessible Registration Form",
    "description": "Build a form with real‑time validation, error messages, and focus management.",
    "estimatedMinutes": 20,
    "problemStatement": "## Accessible Registration Form\n\nBuild an HTML/CSS/JS registration form with the following fields:\n\n* Full name (text, required)\n* Email (email, required)\n* Password (password, required, min 8 characters)\n* Age group (radio group: Under 18, 18–65, 65+)\n* Accept terms (checkbox, required)\n\nThe form must:\n\n1. All inputs have proper labels.\n2. Required fields are marked with an asterisk, and an explanation at the top.\n3. On submit, validate the fields. If errors:\n   - Show an error summary at the top (with `role=\"alert\"`) listing each error and links to the fields.\n   - Set `aria-invalid=\"true\"` on invalid inputs.\n   - Add inline error messages linked via `aria-describedby`.\n   - Focus the error summary.\n4. If validation passes, display a success message (\"Registration successful!\") in place of the form, and focus that message.\n\nUse only vanilla JS. Ensure the form is keyboard and screen reader friendly.",
    "hints": [
        "Use `preventDefault()` on submit to stop page reload.",
        "For the error summary, create a div with `role='alert'` and `tabindex='-1'`, populate its inner HTML, then `focus()` it.",
        "Don't forget to reset `aria-invalid` on fields that are corrected."
    ],
    "expectedOutput": "A functional, accessible registration form.",
    "solutionCode": "<!-- HTML structure (simplified) -->\n<form id=\"reg-form\">\n  <p>Fields marked * are required.</p>\n  <div id=\"error-summary\" role=\"alert\" tabindex=\"-1\" hidden></div>\n\n  <label for=\"name\">Full name *</label>\n  <input type=\"text\" id=\"name\" required aria-describedby=\"name-error\">\n  <span id=\"name-error\" role=\"alert\"></span>\n\n  <label for=\"email\">Email *</label>\n  <input type=\"email\" id=\"email\" required aria-describedby=\"email-error\">\n  <span id=\"email-error\" role=\"alert\"></span>\n\n  <label for=\"password\">Password * (min 8 characters)</label>\n  <input type=\"password\" id=\"password\" required minlength=\"8\" aria-describedby=\"pwd-error\">\n  <span id=\"pwd-error\" role=\"alert\"></span>\n\n  <fieldset>\n    <legend>Age group</legend>\n    <input type=\"radio\" id=\"age1\" name=\"age\" value=\"under18\"><label for=\"age1\">Under 18</label>\n    <input type=\"radio\" id=\"age2\" name=\"age\" value=\"18-65\" checked><label for=\"age2\">18-65</label>\n    <input type=\"radio\" id=\"age3\" name=\"age\" value=\"over65\"><label for=\"age3\">65+</label>\n  </fieldset>\n\n  <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"terms\" required aria-describedby=\"terms-error\">\n  <label for=\"terms\">I accept the terms *</label>\n  <span id=\"terms-error\" role=\"alert\"></span>\n\n  <button type=\"submit\">Register</button>\n</form>\n\n<script>\n  const form = document.getElementById('reg-form');\n  form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {\n    e.preventDefault();\n    // Clear previous errors\n    document.querySelectorAll('[role=\"alert\"]').forEach(el => el.textContent = '');\n    document.querySelectorAll('[aria-invalid]').forEach(el => el.removeAttribute('aria-invalid'));\n    \n    const errors = [];\n    const name = document.getElementById('name');\n    if (name.value.trim() === '') { errors.push({ field: name, msg: 'Enter your name' }); }\n    const email = document.getElementById('email');\n    if (!email.validity.valid) { errors.push({ field: email, msg: 'Enter a valid email' }); }\n    const pwd = document.getElementById('password');\n    if (pwd.value.length < 8) { errors.push({ field: pwd, msg: 'Password must be at least 8 characters' }); }\n    const terms = document.getElementById('terms');\n    if (!terms.checked) { errors.push({ field: terms, msg: 'You must accept the terms' }); }\n\n    if (errors.length > 0) {\n      const summary = document.getElementById('error-summary');\n      summary.hidden = false;\n      summary.innerHTML = '<h2>There is a problem</h2><ul>' + errors.map(e => `<li><a href=\"#${e.field.id}\">${e.msg}</a></li>`).join('') + '</ul>';\n      summary.focus();\n      errors.forEach(e => {\n        e.field.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true');\n        const errorEl = document.getElementById(e.field.getAttribute('aria-describedby'));\n        if (errorEl) errorEl.textContent = e.msg;\n      });\n    } else {\n      form.innerHTML = '<div role=\"alert\" tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"success-msg\"><h2>Registration successful!</h2></div>';\n      document.getElementById('success-msg').focus();\n    }\n  });\n</script>"
}